  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NULL - Bangladesh (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh, Tuberculosis, BRAC (BRAC)This program has the following goals: The goal of Concept note is to reduction of the TB prevalence by 6% by 2017, based on a baseline determined in the prevalence survey to be conducted in 2014. The objectives of this program are: Ensure access to DST for 75% of retreatment cases by 2017; treat 100% of detected MDR-TB cases and achieve a treatment success rate of at least 75% in detected MDR-TB cases.  Ensure adequate support for operational research to foster innovation.  Ensure that 100% of TB service facilities receive regular supervision and monitoring, and produce timely and accurate reports, by 2016.  Ensure that at least 60% of required staff positions identified in a revised national human resource development plan are filled, and 100% of all filled positions are trained, by 2017.  Ensure the long-term availability of 100% of required funding for activities at all program levels through effective planning and partner coordination; maintain GOB contribution greater than 10% of total TB budget.  Increase annual case detection of all forms of TB to 193,687 by 2017 (from baseline of 184,507 in 2013, NTP MIS).  Maintain a treatment success rate of at least 92% in all forms of detected non-MDR TB cases and ensure quality-controlled treatment services at all implementation sites.  Strengthen engagement of all public and private care providers</narrative>
  </description>
